# Vercel serves the static frontend in web/ and nothing else. The Flask app
# runs on Cloud Run - if Vercel sees app.py and requirements.txt it offers to
# deploy them as a Python serverless function, which is the architecture this
# split exists to avoid: a ~4.5 MB request body limit against 150 MB study
# files, and an ephemeral filesystem under a cache that needs to persist.
app.py
etap_reader/
requirements.txt
requirements-hosted.txt
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
read_oti.py
dump_mdf.py
deploy/
docs/
cache/
